# The systemd suite's program fixtures (v1.1 plan, Decision 10; WS-15). Pinned by SHA-256; a case whose fixture is
# missing or not pinned SKIPs with that reason (it never passes), and a fixture that does not match its pin fails
# (CI mounts no fixture, so its cases SKIP: a fixture never blocks a release).
#
# v1.0: no v1.0 release was published, so the fixture is the release program of V10_COMMIT (a commit of the project's
# earlier repository, before it moved here), built with the release build's static Qt. Lay it out as
# <dir>/v1.0/aether-serial-bridge-linux-<arch> and pass driver.py --fixtures <dir>. CI has no copy: its v1.0 cases
# SKIP, and the release checklist asks for them to be run by hand against the pinned files.
V10_COMMIT=ae2f4e99c677f54926b43753c794071a1b528d4b
V10_SHA256_X64=83932caff70e4c0d40dbcd6b777aab96f7c4eea4d3909399085bbbc6b65b7b5b
V10_SHA256_ARM64=76bab0eee1309358ebc5d8bff4d23ed71e6c11d4803ce7398c37c75648320ef2
